"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic","title":"Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","role":"collection"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/alignmentGuide(_:computeValue:)-9thl1":{"kind":"symbol","title":"alignmentGuide(_:computeValue:)","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/alignmentguide(_:computevalue:)-9thl1","role":"symbol","fr